## STEP 2 — KANBAN BOARD
Replace the existing referral table with a Kanban board.
Preserve all existing referral modal functionality exactly 
as it is. The Kanban is only replacing the table view, 
not anything inside the referral modal.

Five columns:
1. New Referral
2. Under Review
3. Waitlisted
4. Accepted
5. Declined

Each column shows a card count in the column header.

Drag and drop between columns updates referral status.
On drop, show a confirmation dialog before committing:
"Move [Patient ID] to [New Status]? 
This will notify the referral source."
Confirm = update status in Supabase + trigger notification.
Cancel = card returns to original column, no state change.

Each referral card displays:
- Patient ID or initials (no full PHI on card face)
- Referral source name and organization
- Date submitted
- Assigned staff member if assigned
- Program tag: Competency / Mental Health / Sober Living / Launch
- Priority badge:
  * EXPEDITED — red
  * TIME-BOUND — orange, show target date e.g. "By 06/15"
  * No badge for standard referrals
- Notification badges:
  * Unread message — blue
  * Unsigned document — amber
  * New attachment — purple
  * Urgent action — red

Clicking a card opens the existing referral modal unchanged.

For the referral source portal:
- Same Kanban component, readOnly prop set to true
- No drag and drop in portal
- Cards show patient name/initials, date, status, 
  unread message badge only
- Summary bar above board:
  "X Active | X Waitlisted | X Accepted | X Declined"
  Clicking a count filters the board to that status
- All data filtered to authenticated referral source 
  only — do not re-implement RLS in frontend

